@byokit/accounts depends on @earendil-works/pi-ai (MIT), which provides the
providers' own sign-in flows. byokit does not modify or redistribute it.

byokit signs a person in to AI plans they already pay for, inside the app they
run it in. Credentials stay in that app's device-owned store and are never logged.

@byokit/usage quota protocol normalization is informed by the MIT-licensed
can1357/oh-my-pi readers at commit 2b023d1 (https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi).
No upstream runtime code or credential discovery is included.

@byokit/accounts' Google Cloud Code Assist sign-in is an independent implementation
of the protocol the Apache-2.0 Gemini CLI client uses; it reuses that client's
public OAuth client id only, with no client secret and no upstream code.

@byokit/accounts' MiniMax user-code sign-in follows the device flow of the
upstream engine's MiniMax extension at 2026.8.1 (MIT-licensed). byokit ships an
independent implementation with no upstream code.
